<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Verden</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Verden is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, historically the seat of a prince-bishopric. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> in 1648, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> received the bishoprics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> and Verden, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wismar">Wismar</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>. These gains gave Sweden territory and votes within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p></div>
